<root>
  <!--
    Arabic interface strings. The name of each entry is the exact English text used in the markup
    inside L["..."]; the value is its Arabic.

    An entry missing here is not an error - the English shows instead. That is what makes this safe to
    fill in gradually, and it is also why LocalizationCoverageTests exists: without a test walking the
    markup and demanding an entry for every string, "falls back to English" quietly becomes permanent.

    Terminology note: prefer the word a KOC colleague would actually say. The technically correct term
    is not always the right one - see the anomaly track, where the dictionary answer for "abnormal"
    carried a slur's connotation in everyday Arabic.
  -->
